-- title:
--   Injectivity on Cartier modules for finite-kernel homomorphisms
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $k$ a field, and let $d,d'$ be natural numbers. Let $\Phi$ be a $d$-dimensional formal group law over $k$, i.e. a $d$-tuple of power series in the variables indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,d \oplus \mathrm{Fin}\,d$ with vanishing constant terms, linear coefficients given by the identity in each block, and satisfying the associativity identity; assume $\Phi$ commutative, i.e. invariant under interchanging the two blocks of variables. Let $\Phi'$ be a commutative $d'$-dimensional formal group law over $k$, and let $\varphi$ be a homomorphism $\Phi \to \Phi'$: a $d'$-tuple $\varphi_1,\dots,\varphi_{d'}$ of power series in $\mathrm{Fin}\,d$ variables with zero constant terms satisfying $\varphi(\Phi(X,Y)) = \Phi'(\varphi(X),\varphi(Y))$. Assume that the quotient of $k[[X_1,\dots,X_d]]$ by the ideal generated by the components $\varphi_i$ is a finite-dimensional $k$-vector space. Then the additive map [`MvFormalGroup.CartierModule.map`](def/MvFormalGroup_CartierModule.html#L739) attached to $\varphi$ is injective; here the Cartier module of $\Phi$ consists of the $d$-tuples $f$ of power series in variables indexed by $\mathbb{N}$ with zero constant terms satisfying $f(S(X;Y)) = \Phi(f(X),f(Y))$, with $S$ the $p$-typical Witt addition polynomials over $k$, and the map sends $f$ to the tuple obtained by substituting $f$ into the components of $\varphi$.
--
--   This is the statement that a homomorphism of commutative formal group laws with finite kernel algebra acts injectively on Cartier modules; specialised to $[p]_\Phi$ for a formal group of finite height it says that the Cartier–Dieudonné module of a $p$-divisible formal group has no $p$-torsion. It is used in the study of special formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-modules, in particular in the length computations for quotients by isogenies of graded submodules and in the parity statement for heights of isogenies over an algebraically closed field.
-- source:
